# Architecture Clusters LLM Guide

## Purpose

Inspect dependency pressure by grouped source areas before editing.

## When To Run

- Before broad refactors.
- When a change may affect many related files.

## How To Read The Result

- Higher pressure suggests more imports, dependents, edges, or lines.
- Incoming and outgoing edges show who relies on the cluster and what it relies on.
- Key files are useful entry points for exploration, not automatic ownership boundaries.

## Examples

- Many incoming edges mean higher blast radius.
- Many outgoing edges may mean too much coordination.
- Small high-pressure clusters may be hidden shared dependencies.

## Agent Tips

- Use this for orientation, not pass/fail validation.
- Prefer lower-pressure areas for incremental work.
- Pair with boundaries before final architecture changes.
